Vendored files: src/*.zig, LICENSE. The upstream build files are kept as
build.zig.upstream / build.zig.zon.upstream for reference only — trm builds
zmx via src/build/GhosttyZmx.zig against the in-tree ghostty-vt module
(src/lib_vt.zig) instead of fetching the upstream ghostty package.

Local patches (record every deviation from upstream here):
- trm's in-tree ghostty-vt Stream.nextSlice returns an error union (the
  upstream-pinned ghostty version did not), so every call site is patched:
  - src/main.zig daemon read loop (~2595): `catch` + warn (must not kill
    the daemon on a state-tracking failure)
  - src/main.zig Daemon.handleOutput (~1165): `try`
  - src/util.zig test helpers/tests (13 sites): `try`
- src/main.zig client accept (~2571): claim leadership on connect when the
  session has none (`if (daemon.leader_client_fd == null) setLeader`).
  Upstream promotes a leader only on *user input* (Daemon.handleInput), and
  only the leader may resize the pty (Daemon.handleResize). A pane restored
  into a session whose previous client disconnected therefore sent its
  geometry to a leaderless daemon, had the resize dropped, and rendered at
  the stale size — unresponsive until someone typed into it, which read as
  trm freezing on restore. Input-based promotion still overrides, so an
  active window reclaims leadership normally.

- src/util.zig serializeTerminalState (~553, ~574): both replay phases
  format with `.unwrap = true` instead of the plain `.vt` preset. Upstream
  replays each grid row terminated with \r\n, which hard-breaks
  soft-wrapped lines in the reattaching client — copying a wrapped URL
  after any reattach picked up newlines the program never printed.
  Unwrapping emits one logical line per wrapped run and lets the client's
  autowrap re-create the wrap flags (and reflow at a different width).
  Covered by test "serializeTerminalState roundtrip preserves soft-wrap
  for copy" in src/util.zig (also a local addition).

To update: clone upstream at a new commit, copy src/*.zig + LICENSE over,
re-apply the patches listed above, update this file, and run
`zig build test` + a manual attach/detach smoke test.
